  "question": {
    "text": "Two ships are sailling in the sea on the two sides of a lighthouse. If the distance between the ships is <math><mn>10</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> meters and their angle of elevations of the top of the lighthouse are <math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math>, then the height of the lighthouse is (The two ships and the foot of lighthouse are in a straight line)"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>20</mn></math> meters",
